  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.13.0 — Add CR1102 (10\" 1280×800 PCAP touchscreen + keypad) device support and a new device-profile abstraction. New namespace Cr1140.Avalonia.Devices with DeviceProfile record (hardware profile: panel dimensions, input capabilities, sysfs/evdev node hints) and DeviceProfiles static class (built-in Cr1140 / Cr1141 / Cr1102 profiles + ByName resolver). EmulatorOptions.ForDevice and EvdevKeypadInput.ForDevice factory methods consume profiles. Output backends (RotatingFbdevOutput / RotatingDrmOutput) are resolution-agnostic: they read the panel mode at runtime, so the 1280×800 CR1102 panel works without library changes. Demo supports --device cr1102|cr1140|cr1141 and CR1140_DEVICE env var. Note: CR1102 low-level sysfs/evdev specifics (keypad device path, backlight max_brightness, thermal zone) are pending on-device confirmation; the datasheet-verified resolution (1280×800) and touch capability are accurate. KeypadKey now covers F1–F8 (F7/F8 added for 8-key SKUs such as the CR1102); the emulator renders the profile's function-key count.",
